          "chunk_id": "34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402-p16-1",
          "page": 16,
          "text": "CPU: Optimize Latency of a Small Number of Complex Threads\n  Five-Stage Instruction Pipeline\n\n¡  Goal: Overlap time of data load/store\n\n¡  Fetch (IF)\n\n   ¡  Get instructions from instruction memory/cache\n\n¡ Decode (ID)\n\n   ¡  Resolve opcode and operands\n¡  Execute (EX)\n\n   ¡  ALU, vector unit, load/store unit, tensor core\n¡ Memory Access (MEM)\n\n   ¡  Load/store data through cache or memory hierarchy\n¡  Write Back (WB)\n\n   ¡  Update architectural state",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402/pages/16/preview",
          "source": "S4"
        },
        {
          "document_id": "34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402",
          "chunk_id": "34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402-p25-1",
          "page": 25,
          "text": "CPU: Optimize Latency of a Small Number of Complex Threads\n  Optimization #3: Out-of-Order (OoO) Execution\n¡  Out-of-order execution separates:\n\n   ¡ Program order: order written by the programmer\n\n   ¡  Execution order: order chosen by hardware\n   ¡ Commit order: order that updates architectural state\n\n\n¡  Typically, the compiler would find independent instruction sets to enable OoO execution, reducing\n   the stall time of the instruction pipeline.\n\n¡ At runtime, CPU involves a controller to find independent instructions while some instructions are\n   waiting.\n\n   ¡  Preempt current pipeline\n\n   ¡  Issue independent instruction\n\n   ¡  Restore preempted instruction when it finishes waiting",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402/pages/25/preview",
          "source": "S5"
